1
00:00:36,430 --> 00:00:38,348
Wow, bro!

2
00:00:38,473 --> 00:00:41,184
I've already told you almost
everything about my life,

3
00:00:41,184 --> 00:00:43,687
and we only just met.

4
00:00:44,088 --> 00:00:45,339
It's just that...

5
00:00:46,398 --> 00:00:49,109
It still hurts, bro, I don't know how—

6
00:00:49,610 --> 00:00:50,944
how she could leave me just like that.

7
00:00:50,944 --> 00:00:52,070
In life,

8
00:00:52,070 --> 00:00:54,448
some people simply have bad luck.

9
00:00:54,948 --> 00:00:56,783
While others are just unbelievably unlucky.

10
00:00:57,034 --> 00:00:58,160
And then there's me,

11
00:00:58,160 --> 00:01:01,288
I've got the premium
subscription to bad luck.

12
00:01:01,913 --> 00:01:02,706
Nope.

13
00:01:02,831 --> 00:01:03,932
That's not me.

14
00:01:03,957 --> 00:01:05,292
Unlucky, right?

15
00:01:05,834 --> 00:01:06,975
This is a hold-up.

16
00:01:07,186 --> 00:01:08,145
Give me your wallet!

17
00:01:08,170 --> 00:01:08,962
There.

18
00:01:09,046 --> 00:01:09,890
That's me.

19
00:01:10,020 --> 00:01:13,812
Still handsome, right? Even if bad
luck will soon beat me up.

20
00:01:13,842 --> 00:01:15,302
Is there a camera around—

21
00:01:15,302 --> 00:01:16,903
Bro, is this a prank?

22
00:01:16,928 --> 00:01:18,388
This has to be a prank.

23
00:01:19,306 --> 00:01:20,307
Give me your wallet.

24
00:01:21,350 --> 00:01:22,171
Uh—

25
00:01:22,392 --> 00:01:23,769
You know what, bro?

26
00:01:24,019 --> 00:01:26,104
If only I weren't drunk, I would—

27
00:01:26,104 --> 00:01:27,505
I said give me your wallet!

28
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:32,841
Give me that!

29
00:01:33,028 --> 00:01:34,068
Give me that!

30
00:01:36,406 --> 00:01:38,008
Ouch.

31
00:01:38,033 --> 00:01:39,107
Give me your wallet!

32
00:01:41,370 --> 00:01:43,121
Ouch!

33
00:01:44,122 --> 00:01:45,165
You're such bad luck!

34
00:01:45,374 --> 00:01:47,834
Is it my fault your
mugging isn't paying off?

35
00:01:48,126 --> 00:01:50,479
If only you'd gotten an honest job.

36
00:01:50,504 --> 00:01:53,340
- You think you're smarter than me, huh?
- No, I was just joking.

37
00:01:54,174 --> 00:01:55,467
But would you believe it,

38
00:01:55,759 --> 00:01:58,720
on the day I thought
I couldn't get any unluckier...

39
00:01:58,929 --> 00:02:00,055
I met you.

40
00:02:00,347 --> 00:02:02,265
You didn't just bring me a stroke of luck.

41
00:02:02,891 --> 00:02:04,309
You brought a whole lot of it.

42
00:02:04,309 --> 00:02:05,560
As in, lots.

43
00:02:05,560 --> 00:02:07,145
Hey!

44
00:03:33,273 --> 00:03:34,357
Jean!

45
00:03:34,941 --> 00:03:36,651
Really, Jean?

46
00:03:36,777 --> 00:03:38,653
I miss you, Jean!

47
00:03:39,112 --> 00:03:40,989
This is the guy you see
a future with, Jean?

48
00:03:40,989 --> 00:03:41,990
Not with me?

49
00:03:44,868 --> 00:03:46,620
I'm not trying to be rude, but...

50
00:03:46,703 --> 00:03:48,955
I'm way better looking than this guy!

51
00:03:50,290 --> 00:03:51,958
He looks old enough to be your dad.

52
00:03:52,459 --> 00:03:53,350
Ugh!

53
00:03:54,075 --> 00:03:55,493
I'm not bitter or anything, Jean.

54
00:03:56,797 --> 00:03:57,858
Actually...

55
00:03:58,013 --> 00:03:59,640
I'm happy for you.

56
00:04:00,717 --> 00:04:01,467
Popsy...

57
00:04:02,752 --> 00:04:03,878
that's getting pretty bad.

58
00:04:04,471 --> 00:04:05,592
You need to talk to him.

59
00:04:05,972 --> 00:04:07,524
He's embarrassing us
in front of the customers.

60
00:04:07,548 --> 00:04:08,058
Jean!

61
00:04:08,276 --> 00:04:12,061
Looks like Estong really
got that from his mother.

62
00:04:12,896 --> 00:04:14,397
Too emotional.

63
00:04:15,291 --> 00:04:19,022
Well, at least his mother's moved on—
in heaven.

64
00:04:19,569 --> 00:04:20,862
Rest in peace, my love.

65
00:04:22,838 --> 00:04:24,799
Oh, speaking of mothers.

66
00:04:24,825 --> 00:04:27,410
Have you talked to your Momsy Janet yet?

67
00:04:27,953 --> 00:04:29,704
Uh...not yet, Popsy.

68
00:04:30,097 --> 00:04:31,473
Maybe later.

69
00:04:31,498 --> 00:04:33,250
It's still 5 PM there in Sydney,

70
00:04:33,250 --> 00:04:35,085
- so Momsy might still be at work.
- Oh, right.

71
00:04:35,858 --> 00:04:37,087
Hey, remind her, okay?

72
00:04:37,087 --> 00:04:42,428
Don't forget to help your Kuya Estong
find a job in Australia, okay?

73
00:04:42,717 --> 00:04:45,387
Maybe there, he can finally move on.

74
00:04:48,014 --> 00:04:51,351
Jean!

75
00:04:51,793 --> 00:04:54,253
Are you really never
coming back to me, Jean?

76
00:04:56,356 --> 00:04:57,107
Jean, please!

77
00:04:57,107 --> 00:04:58,066
Just a sec, please.

78
00:04:58,358 --> 00:05:00,277
Jean!

79
00:05:00,402 --> 00:05:02,362
I really can't accept this.

80
00:05:02,362 --> 00:05:04,072
- Kuya.
- Jean!

81
00:05:07,284 --> 00:05:08,827
What have you done, bro?

82
00:05:09,050 --> 00:05:10,051
Kuya.

83
00:05:10,178 --> 00:05:12,138
You can't stay like this forever.

84
00:05:12,163 --> 00:05:14,416
That's why you're here, right?

85
00:05:14,569 --> 00:05:16,279
Unpack your baggage already.

86
00:05:22,841 --> 00:05:24,438
I can't do this anymore.
I don't want to live.

87
00:05:24,462 --> 00:05:25,594
Hey, stop it. Knock it off.

88
00:05:25,594 --> 00:05:26,303
Kuya.

89
00:05:26,303 --> 00:05:27,804
I can't breathe.

90
00:05:27,804 --> 00:05:30,181
Well, obviously. Stop choking yourself.

91
00:05:30,348 --> 00:05:31,741
- Hey!
- Just let it go!

92
00:05:31,766 --> 00:05:32,796
Jestoni!

93
00:05:33,442 --> 00:05:35,986
Remember, in this family,

94
00:05:36,453 --> 00:05:37,662
we never give up.

95
00:05:39,820 --> 00:05:40,988
As long as there's breath in us,

96
00:05:41,067 --> 00:05:42,694
there's still fight in us.

97
00:05:42,736 --> 00:05:44,062
Exactly.

98
00:05:45,071 --> 00:05:46,171
You know what,

99
00:05:46,748 --> 00:05:47,957
you're right, Popsy Bert.

100
00:05:50,956 --> 00:05:52,166
I need to let this out.

101
00:05:53,163 --> 00:05:54,055
Hey!

102
00:05:54,080 --> 00:05:54,710
Hey!

103
00:05:54,831 --> 00:05:56,082
- Kuya.
- Hey! Estong!

104
00:05:56,333 --> 00:05:57,459
Hey.

105
00:05:57,924 --> 00:05:59,843
Jean, I'm gonna forget you!

106
00:05:59,936 --> 00:06:01,450
This will be the last day
I'll ever say your name!

107
00:06:01,474 --> 00:06:02,147
Please excuse us.

108
00:06:02,172 --> 00:06:03,815
I can survive on my own!

109
00:06:03,840 --> 00:06:05,508
She can't hear you from here, Kuya.

110
00:06:19,773 --> 00:06:22,655
- I can't survive on my own!
- Hey, relax!

111
00:06:22,994 --> 00:06:24,829
I need someone, Pops!

112
00:06:24,861 --> 00:06:25,820
Why don't you just jump?

113
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:26,741
No, don't!

114
00:06:27,185 --> 00:06:29,514
- This is so hard!
- Come on, let's get back inside.

115
00:06:31,201 --> 00:06:33,119
- Miss!
- Yeah, pull him back, Popsy.

116
00:06:33,144 --> 00:06:34,429
Life is so hard!

117
00:06:34,454 --> 00:06:35,872
Life is so hard!

118
00:06:36,046 --> 00:06:37,506
Let me stay here.

119
00:06:37,624 --> 00:06:38,708
- You're so heavy, Kuya.
- I want to jump.

120
00:06:38,708 --> 00:06:39,678
Excuse us, Miss.

121
00:06:47,676 --> 00:06:49,103
Not now.

122
00:06:49,594 --> 00:06:51,012
Please, not now.

123
00:06:51,734 --> 00:06:52,776
I can't do this now.

124
00:06:56,935 --> 00:06:58,895
Cheers!

125
00:06:59,229 --> 00:07:00,981
That's what I'm talking about.

126
00:07:01,690 --> 00:07:03,191
These are my friends.

127
00:07:03,191 --> 00:07:05,860
I just met these guys today. Wow.

128
00:07:06,319 --> 00:07:10,573
They've really been listening to me...
to what I've been through.

129
00:07:11,042 --> 00:07:12,960
- I'm letting you go, Jean!
- You've got this.

130
00:07:13,076 --> 00:07:14,244
Hang in there,

131
00:07:14,911 --> 00:07:16,121
Whatever makes you happy.

132
00:07:16,871 --> 00:07:18,748
This guy's like a brother to me.

133
00:07:18,972 --> 00:07:20,181
Thank you, bro.

134
00:07:22,168 --> 00:07:23,860
- Ah, Jean.
- Oh, man.

135
00:07:24,045 --> 00:07:25,964
- Someone's still making a scene.
- Bro, I'm trying to move on.

136
00:07:25,964 --> 00:07:28,800
Bro, I can't do this anymore.
Promise, I really can't.

137
00:07:29,805 --> 00:07:31,599
I'm going to move on, bro.

138
00:07:31,825 --> 00:07:32,860
Jean!

139
00:07:33,638 --> 00:07:35,056
I love you, Jean!

140
00:07:35,056 --> 00:07:38,059
- I miss you so much, Jean!
- Oh, man.

141
00:07:39,436 --> 00:07:42,439
Jestoni, head home.
Something might happen to you!

142
00:07:42,605 --> 00:07:45,275
Jayden, hurry up. You still have
something to deliver.

143
00:07:45,859 --> 00:07:47,681
Bro, is this a prank?

144
00:07:47,983 --> 00:07:49,276
This has to be a prank.

145
00:07:50,030 --> 00:07:51,306
Give me your wallet.

146
00:07:53,190 --> 00:07:54,805
You know what, bro?

147
00:07:55,134 --> 00:07:56,995
If only I weren't drunk, I would—

148
00:07:56,995 --> 00:07:58,485
I said give me your wallet!

149
00:08:02,883 --> 00:08:03,550
Give me that!

150
00:08:03,678 --> 00:08:04,845
Give me that!

151
00:08:07,422 --> 00:08:08,189
Ouch.

152
00:08:08,923 --> 00:08:09,962
Give me your wallet!

153
00:08:12,553 --> 00:08:14,180
It hurts!

154
00:08:14,374 --> 00:08:15,500
It hurts!

155
00:08:17,772 --> 00:08:19,111
You're such bad luck!

156
00:08:19,136 --> 00:08:20,137
Tell me about it!

157
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:23,626
Is it my fault your
mugging isn't paying off?

158
00:08:23,659 --> 00:08:25,744
If only you'd gotten an honest job.

159
00:08:25,857 --> 00:08:27,358
You think you're smarter than me, huh?

160
00:08:27,358 --> 00:08:28,439
It's just a joke.

161
00:08:36,635 --> 00:08:37,696
Hey!

162
00:08:40,872 --> 00:08:42,743
Yup, that's me.

163
00:08:42,957 --> 00:08:45,060
This was supposed to
be a calm night for me.

164
00:08:45,227 --> 00:08:47,350
But then I got caught up in this mess.

165
00:08:47,375 --> 00:08:49,210
How did I end up here?

166
00:08:49,489 --> 00:08:51,587
Oh my, I need to go out.

167
00:08:51,925 --> 00:08:53,777
Ysa, I don't want to go out.

168
00:08:53,802 --> 00:08:58,389
We need to go out.
So we can finish this and submit it!

169
00:08:58,389 --> 00:09:02,393
My dear, always be careful outside.

170
00:09:02,393 --> 00:09:05,605
Leave it to me.
No one will dare hurt us!

171
00:09:05,605 --> 00:09:07,607
Calm down. All of us should relax.

172
00:09:07,607 --> 00:09:10,383
O, to the M, to the G! Let's go already!

173
00:09:10,408 --> 00:09:11,868
Thank you! Come again, okay?

174
00:09:11,986 --> 00:09:13,087
See you tomorrow!

175
00:09:14,097 --> 00:09:14,890
Okay!

176
00:09:16,282 --> 00:09:17,509
Okay.

177
00:09:17,534 --> 00:09:19,327
Um...do you have any cooked rice?

178
00:09:22,263 --> 00:09:23,889
Love, please hold me back.

179
00:09:23,914 --> 00:09:25,324
Don't make me put him in a rice sack.

180
00:09:27,268 --> 00:09:29,020
We don't sell that here.

181
00:09:29,145 --> 00:09:30,730
Try checking eatery down the street.

182
00:09:30,895 --> 00:09:31,980
Oh, all right.

183
00:09:33,216 --> 00:09:36,219
Excuse me! Gorgeous coming through!

184
00:09:36,219 --> 00:09:38,840
- The artist is on the way!
- Hey, Ysa! Ysa! Oh, I mean...

185
00:09:39,324 --> 00:09:40,223
Cacai! Cacai!

186
00:09:40,248 --> 00:09:42,492
- So hot here!
- Sweetheart, wait, just a second!

187
00:09:42,532 --> 00:09:44,285
Why are you such in a hurry?

188
00:09:44,310 --> 00:09:47,268
Nonong, Nanang,
the pressure is so pressuring!

189
00:09:47,293 --> 00:09:49,211
Oh my Gosh, really!

190
00:09:49,236 --> 00:09:50,321
What did she say?

191
00:09:51,817 --> 00:09:53,002
Listen, sweetheart.

192
00:09:53,127 --> 00:09:54,879
I understand.

193
00:09:54,904 --> 00:09:57,198
It's okay to be super girly.

194
00:09:57,198 --> 00:09:59,200
But calm down. Just calm down.

195
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:00,869
Here, I'm going to give you something.

196
00:10:01,619 --> 00:10:02,203
Here.

197
00:10:02,203 --> 00:10:03,324
Oh, I forgot something.

198
00:10:08,751 --> 00:10:09,335
Here, let's put it back.

199
00:10:09,335 --> 00:10:13,214
Because Nang, I still have that
painting deadline for Ms. Amara.

200
00:10:13,214 --> 00:10:15,425
If I fail, if I flop—

201
00:10:15,425 --> 00:10:18,011
Oh no, I can already feel the failure.

202
00:10:18,011 --> 00:10:19,470
I don't like failure!

203
00:10:19,470 --> 00:10:21,097
It's okay, my sweetheart. It's okay.

204
00:10:21,097 --> 00:10:24,434
Oh, one more thing.
Don't forget this. Drink this, okay?

205
00:10:24,434 --> 00:10:25,518
This is for your anxiety.

206
00:10:25,518 --> 00:10:27,187
Here, put everything in your bag.

207
00:10:27,187 --> 00:10:27,937
Okay, thank you!

208
00:10:27,937 --> 00:10:29,147
Alright, take care, okay?

209
00:10:29,147 --> 00:10:29,939
- Bye!
- Okay.

210
00:10:29,939 --> 00:10:31,649
- Bye, bye! Goodluck!
- Bye Nong, bye Nang!

211
00:10:31,649 --> 00:10:33,735
- Cacai, wait!
- Hello!

212
00:10:34,834 --> 00:10:36,878
- Hello, good morning!
- Hi, Ysa!

213
00:10:41,242 --> 00:10:42,994
That timing of the ice cream guy!

214
00:10:43,220 --> 00:10:45,556
Ice cream!

215
00:10:46,122 --> 00:10:47,874
- Mister, mister! One ice cream please.
- I want ice cream!

216
00:10:47,874 --> 00:10:49,792
Yeye wants ice cream.

217
00:10:50,084 --> 00:10:52,545
Wow! Thank you!

218
00:10:53,713 --> 00:10:55,882
- Mmmm!
- Alright, take it easy.

219
00:10:56,758 --> 00:11:00,178
My dear, you forgot your fidget toy,
the one that helps with your stress.

220
00:11:01,346 --> 00:11:02,355
Thank you!

221
00:11:05,308 --> 00:11:08,019
Hello, hello, Nagkaisang Neighbors!

222
00:11:09,979 --> 00:11:10,769
Adel.

223
00:11:11,589 --> 00:11:12,923
Um, it's just that...

224
00:11:13,775 --> 00:11:18,238
Number One has to finish a painting because
she needs to submit it to Ms. Amara today.

225
00:11:18,238 --> 00:11:20,782
But Number Two suddenly came out.

226
00:11:21,532 --> 00:11:22,941
Leave this to me, Ninang B

227
00:11:26,019 --> 00:11:27,604
Hello, Yeye!

228
00:11:27,629 --> 00:11:29,047
Come on, let's do our handshake.

229
00:11:31,459 --> 00:11:33,211
- Ice cream?
- I'm good, it's all yours.

230
00:11:34,103 --> 00:11:35,855
You seem pretty busy lately.

231
00:11:36,036 --> 00:11:39,164
How about we go to
your favorite playground?

232
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:41,611
- Playground.
- Wanna go?

233
00:11:41,729 --> 00:11:42,832
Let's go?

234
00:11:43,179 --> 00:11:45,056
- You guys want to—
- Yeye wants to play.

235
00:11:45,056 --> 00:11:46,266
Come on, let's go?

236
00:11:46,408 --> 00:11:47,450
I can take you guys there, if you want.

237
00:11:47,475 --> 00:11:49,894
No need, Ninong K. We'll just run.

238
00:11:49,894 --> 00:11:52,519
So, wanna make it a
race? One, two, three...

239
00:11:52,772 --> 00:11:54,857
- Go! Come on!
- Huh?

240
00:12:14,961 --> 00:12:16,644
Are you sure you're okay, Ate?

241
00:12:17,088 --> 00:12:17,797
Hm?

242
00:12:19,590 --> 00:12:20,746
Of course.

243
00:12:20,925 --> 00:12:21,949
I'm okay now.

244
00:12:23,539 --> 00:12:25,291
I don't mind waiting here.

245
00:12:25,773 --> 00:12:28,408
I don't really have much
going on today, so...

246
00:12:28,589 --> 00:12:30,174
I can just make sure you're safe.

247
00:12:31,807 --> 00:12:34,035
I'll be okay. I can take care of myself.

248
00:12:34,605 --> 00:12:36,065
But thank you for the concern.

249
00:12:36,065 --> 00:12:38,401
I just need to finish this painting

250
00:12:38,401 --> 00:12:41,254
because I have to submit
it to Ms. Amara later.

251
00:12:41,279 --> 00:12:43,504
But really, thank you for
looking out for me, Adel.

252
00:12:44,109 --> 00:12:45,068
You promise?

253
00:12:47,285 --> 00:12:48,328
I can manage, I promise.

254
00:12:50,663 --> 00:12:52,081
Just text me, okay?

255
00:12:52,081 --> 00:12:53,041
Sure, I'll text you.

256
00:12:53,041 --> 00:12:54,066
Alright, you take care.

257
00:13:01,257 --> 00:13:02,277
Ma'am,

258
00:13:02,759 --> 00:13:05,472
here is your coffee.

259
00:13:07,952 --> 00:13:08,953
Thank you.

260
00:13:10,651 --> 00:13:11,485
Thank you.

261
00:13:13,218 --> 00:13:14,285
Thank you.

262
00:13:17,857 --> 00:13:21,110
A painting is made up
of different elements.

263
00:13:21,709 --> 00:13:23,377
There are straight lines

264
00:13:23,557 --> 00:13:24,766
and curved ones.

265
00:13:25,299 --> 00:13:27,050
There are different shapes

266
00:13:27,686 --> 00:13:30,063
and colors that complement each other,

267
00:13:30,344 --> 00:13:32,472
and there are other
things you can blend in.

268
00:13:33,014 --> 00:13:35,183
All these combined elements...

269
00:13:35,208 --> 00:13:37,057
give it depth,

270
00:13:37,082 --> 00:13:37,960
character,

271
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:39,087
and beauty.

272
00:13:39,253 --> 00:13:41,547
And when you look at it as a whole,

273
00:13:41,547 --> 00:13:44,300
the differences just fade away...

274
00:13:44,300 --> 00:13:47,887
because all you see
is the complete picture.

275
00:13:47,887 --> 00:13:49,086
Just like people.

276
00:13:49,111 --> 00:13:50,990
We all have different memories...

277
00:13:51,170 --> 00:13:52,213
emotions,

278
00:13:52,633 --> 00:13:53,968
experiences,

279
00:13:53,993 --> 00:13:55,286
and decisions.

280
00:13:55,576 --> 00:13:57,703
They all shape who we are.

281
00:13:58,106 --> 00:14:00,647
We're all like blank
canvasses from the start.

282
00:14:01,067 --> 00:14:02,360
But as time goes by...

283
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:03,928
our picture begins to take shape.

284
00:14:05,488 --> 00:14:09,283
And even if there are parts of ourselves
we don't understand...

285
00:14:13,913 --> 00:14:16,332
the parts that feel
like they don't belong...

286
00:14:17,375 --> 00:14:19,871
the parts that don't make sense—

287
00:14:20,211 --> 00:14:21,379
The truth is,

288
00:14:22,088 --> 00:14:24,261
all of us are works in progress.

289
00:14:24,424 --> 00:14:29,433
- And soon... you'll finally see the whole picture.
- Jean, I'm now going to forget you!

290
00:14:34,725 --> 00:14:36,310
Let me stay here!

291
00:14:36,602 --> 00:14:37,687
- I want to jump!
- You're so heavy.

292
00:14:37,687 --> 00:14:39,021
Excuse us, miss.

293
00:14:46,529 --> 00:14:47,879
Not now.

294
00:14:48,406 --> 00:14:49,991
Please, not now.

295
00:14:59,372 --> 00:15:01,124
All done. You'd never notice it now.

296
00:15:02,044 --> 00:15:03,879
Like it's just part of the painting now.

297
00:15:14,849 --> 00:15:16,992
Hello, Ysabelle?

298
00:15:17,017 --> 00:15:18,268
Hello, Ms. Amara.

299
00:15:19,228 --> 00:15:21,939
I've finished the painting.
I'll bring it to you now.

300
00:15:23,441 --> 00:15:26,652
I'm really sorry, I thought
I'd miss the deadline.

301
00:15:27,695 --> 00:15:29,918
Oh no, don't worry about it.

302
00:15:31,781 --> 00:15:32,707
I'm sorry?

303
00:15:33,493 --> 00:15:36,370
Actually, I had a family emergency.

304
00:15:36,370 --> 00:15:37,997
The schedule got moved.

305
00:15:38,456 --> 00:15:42,376
If it's okay with you, you can
send it to me after two days.

306
00:15:43,087 --> 00:15:43,838
Oh.

307
00:15:44,409 --> 00:15:45,494
I see.

308
00:15:47,131 --> 00:15:48,799
So, you don't need the painting right now?

309
00:15:48,799 --> 00:15:52,862
Yes. No rush. You can still perfect it.

310
00:15:52,887 --> 00:15:54,430
Oh, alright.

311
00:15:54,805 --> 00:15:55,854
Thank you so much.

312
00:15:55,879 --> 00:15:58,059
Okay, just update me.

313
00:15:58,100 --> 00:15:58,777
Bye-bye!

314
00:15:58,802 --> 00:16:00,019
Bye.

315
00:16:33,601 --> 00:16:34,769
Give it to me!

316
00:16:38,432 --> 00:16:39,392
You're such a bad luck!

317
00:16:39,392 --> 00:16:41,602
Is it my fault your
mugging isn't paying off?

318
00:16:41,602 --> 00:16:43,660
- You think you're smarter than me, huh?
- You will not bring her with you.

319
00:16:47,233 --> 00:16:49,110
Hey!

320
00:16:56,151 --> 00:16:57,319
Why are you butting in?

321
00:16:57,344 --> 00:16:59,137
I'm going to forget you, Jean!

322
00:17:05,803 --> 00:17:07,121
You're such a meddler!

323
00:17:09,178 --> 00:17:10,113
What?!

324
00:17:11,425 --> 00:17:13,177
No more! I'm done!

325
00:17:18,357 --> 00:17:19,151
That jerk.

326
00:17:19,724 --> 00:17:20,975
Oh, wait, miss...

327
00:17:21,267 --> 00:17:22,324
- What?
- Miss...

328
00:17:24,228 --> 00:17:25,646
Thank you...

329
00:17:30,634 --> 00:17:32,553
Oh my God, I'm so sorry!

330
00:17:36,695 --> 00:17:38,197
You're not my type, bro.

331
00:17:39,187 --> 00:17:40,605
Ow, that hurts!

332
00:17:45,218 --> 00:17:46,761
Bro, what's this? Check it out.

333
00:17:46,786 --> 00:17:47,808
Let me see.

334
00:17:48,044 --> 00:17:50,171
- Maybe there's something important in it.
- Whoa, bro. It's a painting.

335
00:17:50,171 --> 00:17:52,715
- Nice! We could sell that, dude.
- Hey, that's not yours!

336
00:17:52,715 --> 00:17:54,842
- Let's make some money. Hurry!
- Don't.

337
00:18:00,723 --> 00:18:01,766
Come on.

338
00:18:02,499 --> 00:18:03,876
Oh no. My son!

339
00:18:05,227 --> 00:18:06,646
Ow!

340
00:18:07,938 --> 00:18:12,276
- Aww, poor you.
- Take it easy.

341
00:18:12,276 --> 00:18:14,570
The survivor's finally awake.

342
00:18:15,780 --> 00:18:16,906
Bro, what happened?

343
00:18:16,989 --> 00:18:18,082
Pops, what happened?

344
00:18:18,693 --> 00:18:19,902
How did I get home?

345
00:18:20,826 --> 00:18:22,078
Oh my. I'm sorry.

346
00:18:22,078 --> 00:18:23,324
Come on, Pops.

347
00:18:24,330 --> 00:18:26,480
We should be the ones asking you that.

348
00:18:26,682 --> 00:18:29,226
My barangay security
officer buddies called me.

349
00:18:29,444 --> 00:18:32,322
They said they saw you
sprawled out in some alley.

350
00:18:32,347 --> 00:18:33,891
They said it looked like a crime scene.

351
00:18:36,717 --> 00:18:38,135
Pops, I got mugged.

352
00:18:38,624 --> 00:18:40,125
I thought I was going to die.

353
00:18:40,817 --> 00:18:42,944
Luckily, a woman came by and saved me.

354
00:18:44,839 --> 00:18:45,923
Like an angel?

355
00:18:47,328 --> 00:18:49,080
I don't know bro, she also punched me.

356
00:18:49,105 --> 00:18:49,933
Oh.

357
00:18:50,360 --> 00:18:53,292
Wait a minute. I'm confused.

358
00:18:53,481 --> 00:18:56,067
She saved you, then she punched you?

359
00:18:56,643 --> 00:18:58,910
Because I threw up on her, Pops.

360
00:18:58,948 --> 00:19:00,048
You threw up?

361
00:19:00,157 --> 00:19:01,509
That explains it, Kuya.

362
00:19:01,534 --> 00:19:02,816
It was also your fault.

363
00:19:03,637 --> 00:19:05,263
I didn't mean to do it, bro.

364
00:19:06,414 --> 00:19:07,540
After that,

365
00:19:09,114 --> 00:19:10,323
she just disappeared.

366
00:19:11,544 --> 00:19:13,462
I wonder where that strange woman is from.

367
00:19:20,010 --> 00:19:20,977
Alright, bro.

368
00:19:21,002 --> 00:19:23,129
Try to find her first thing in the morning.

369
00:19:23,377 --> 00:19:24,837
So you can get beaten up even more.

370
00:19:25,808 --> 00:19:27,601
Oh, stop. Can't you
see he's in a lot of pain?

371
00:19:27,601 --> 00:19:28,519
Ow!

372
00:19:28,544 --> 00:19:31,338
- Such a shame I didn't get to see it.
- Alright, take it easy.

373
00:19:36,512 --> 00:19:37,930
Where did I put it?

374
00:19:43,909 --> 00:19:44,701
Where is it?

375
00:19:53,399 --> 00:19:56,694
I hope someone wrote an entry, I hope
someone wrote an entry.

376
00:20:11,689 --> 00:20:13,148
Where is my painting?

377
00:20:13,397 --> 00:20:16,484
What if I lost it? I can't lose it. I
have to find it, or I'm in trouble.

378
00:20:16,822 --> 00:20:18,980
I'm supposed to give it to Ms. Amara.

379
00:20:20,112 --> 00:20:21,405
I hope they can remember it.

380
00:20:21,781 --> 00:20:22,738
I hope...

381
00:20:24,314 --> 00:20:25,440
Ysa?

382
00:20:26,120 --> 00:20:26,954
Are you okay?

383
00:20:28,114 --> 00:20:29,263
Dear.

384
00:20:29,420 --> 00:20:30,546
Looks like you got home late.

385
00:20:31,207 --> 00:20:32,183
Uh...

386
00:20:32,403 --> 00:20:35,572
I was finishing the painting that
Ms. Amara commissioned.

387
00:20:36,170 --> 00:20:37,146
Painting.

388
00:20:37,171 --> 00:20:39,540
Wow! You finished your painting?

389
00:20:39,565 --> 00:20:40,900
You didn't even bother to text us?

390
00:20:40,925 --> 00:20:41,776
Huh?

391
00:20:41,801 --> 00:20:42,426
Oh.

392
00:20:42,691 --> 00:20:44,261
I had to frame it first.

393
00:20:44,345 --> 00:20:47,285
Wait, I thought the
painting was due yesterday?

394
00:20:48,182 --> 00:20:49,325
It got moved.

395
00:20:49,350 --> 00:20:50,117
Uh...

396
00:20:50,142 --> 00:20:51,949
That's why I need to pick it up tomorrow.

397
00:20:52,697 --> 00:20:53,656
I'll come with you!

398
00:20:53,837 --> 00:20:55,797
I want to see the finished
product right away.

399
00:20:56,672 --> 00:20:57,527
Huh?

400
00:20:59,001 --> 00:21:01,420
Oh, no, there's no need! Well, um...

401
00:21:01,445 --> 00:21:03,197
Why don't you all go together with Nonong,

402
00:21:03,197 --> 00:21:06,450
so... the more the
merrier. Isn't that right?

403
00:21:07,660 --> 00:21:09,535
You know, sweetheart,
we're so proud of you.

404
00:21:10,574 --> 00:21:13,285
I'm sure Ate Ysa's other
selves are happy too.

405
00:21:13,374 --> 00:21:14,277
Exactly.

406
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:16,733
Most of her other selves share her passion.

407
00:21:16,836 --> 00:21:20,172
But I hope you can also teach your minority
selves about painting,

408
00:21:20,711 --> 00:21:22,379
so you can all be one.

409
00:21:22,591 --> 00:21:24,510
The more complete,
the happier you'll be.

410
00:21:26,762 --> 00:21:31,684
Ysa, sweetheart, thank you for everything
you've done, most especially for Belle.

411
00:21:35,145 --> 00:21:36,497
Ysa, are you okay?

412
00:21:36,522 --> 00:21:37,248
Dear?

413
00:21:37,273 --> 00:21:38,774
Could you get her some water?

414
00:21:39,525 --> 00:21:40,901
Come on, take a seat.

415
00:21:40,985 --> 00:21:41,902
Get the brush.

416
00:21:43,153 --> 00:21:43,904
Dear?

417
00:21:45,698 --> 00:21:46,699
Are you okay?

418
00:21:47,324 --> 00:21:48,367
Here, drink some water.

419
00:21:48,367 --> 00:21:49,660
Come on, have a drink.

420
00:21:51,453 --> 00:21:52,121
Here.

421
00:21:53,873 --> 00:21:54,582
Here, Ysa.

422
00:21:55,590 --> 00:21:56,292
- Hold it.
- Here, Ysa.

423
00:21:56,767 --> 00:21:58,060
Just focus on the brush.

424
00:21:58,085 --> 00:22:00,296
Breathe. Take a deep breath.

425
00:22:01,380 --> 00:22:03,090
Breathe, Ysa.

426
00:22:04,900 --> 00:22:05,609
Go on.

427
00:22:05,821 --> 00:22:06,655
You're okay.

428
00:22:11,074 --> 00:22:11,783
Um...

429
00:22:14,284 --> 00:22:16,412
I'll get going now, Auntie.

430
00:22:16,437 --> 00:22:19,301
Uh...I'm okay. I just
got a little too excited.

431
00:22:19,741 --> 00:22:20,708
Wait.

432
00:22:20,733 --> 00:22:21,834
Ysa.

433
00:22:21,859 --> 00:22:24,194
I'm fine, really. I just got too excited.

434
00:22:24,194 --> 00:22:25,237
- Are you sure?
- I need to go now.

435
00:22:25,237 --> 00:22:27,318
- You don't need me to come with you?
- Yes, yes.

436
00:22:27,343 --> 00:22:28,511
No, I'll be okay. Bye!

437
00:22:29,464 --> 00:22:30,883
Dear, you take care okay?

438
00:22:44,239 --> 00:22:45,949
Where did my painting go?

439
00:23:04,192 --> 00:23:06,194
I knew you would be coming back here.

440
00:23:15,734 --> 00:23:16,568
Uh, miss.

441
00:23:17,613 --> 00:23:20,407
Miss, I just want to say thank
you for saving me from that mugger.

442
00:23:23,364 --> 00:23:24,991
But your punch was too much.

443
00:23:26,135 --> 00:23:30,199
I almost ended up in the hospital
to join my mom in heaven.

444
00:23:35,599 --> 00:23:36,933
Bogart.

445
00:23:38,442 --> 00:23:39,818
That was not me.

446
00:23:41,722 --> 00:23:42,738
Miss...

447
00:23:43,165 --> 00:23:44,291
I was only drunk.

448
00:23:44,535 --> 00:23:47,628
But I'm not blind, and I'm
not that old to be senile.

449
00:23:47,746 --> 00:23:49,433
That really wasn't me, Kuya.

450
00:23:49,458 --> 00:23:50,501
How can that be?

451
00:23:51,067 --> 00:23:53,069
Why? Do you have a twin?

452
00:23:54,464 --> 00:23:55,590
There, see?

453
00:23:59,622 --> 00:24:02,792
Gosh, my painting.
Where is my painting?

454
00:24:03,401 --> 00:24:04,730
Oh, the painting?

455
00:24:04,781 --> 00:24:06,057
You took my painting?

456
00:24:06,082 --> 00:24:07,144
Not me.

457
00:24:07,356 --> 00:24:09,108
I was the one who got mugged.

458
00:24:09,421 --> 00:24:11,238
The mugger took my painting?

459
00:24:12,903 --> 00:24:14,488
Uh...

460
00:24:14,794 --> 00:24:16,296
Someone else took it.

461
00:24:17,489 --> 00:24:19,866
But...what if they're accomplices?

462
00:24:20,586 --> 00:24:22,046
Well, I didn't see their faces because...

463
00:24:22,569 --> 00:24:26,156
The alcohol packed a punch, and so did you.

464
00:24:28,318 --> 00:24:30,529
If you're not going to help me,

465
00:24:30,529 --> 00:24:32,031
then stop bothering me.

466
00:24:32,031 --> 00:24:33,785
I have to find my painting.

467
00:24:47,574 --> 00:24:48,450
Oh, ma'am...

468
00:24:48,538 --> 00:24:51,668
We can't just simply hand out CCTV footage.

469
00:24:51,876 --> 00:24:55,129
You'll need a police report before
we can process your request.

470
00:24:56,244 --> 00:24:57,871
That's our standard procedure.

471
00:25:00,934 --> 00:25:02,061
Jennelyn. What is Ysa doing here?

472
00:25:02,061 --> 00:25:04,291
Come on, take a photo, quick!

473
00:25:04,316 --> 00:25:05,731
Then let's send it to our group chat.

474
00:25:05,731 --> 00:25:09,019
Okay, let's go. We'll be late for bingo.

475
00:25:09,232 --> 00:25:11,943
Alright, sir. I'll just come back.

476
00:25:12,641 --> 00:25:13,392
Thank you.

477
00:25:26,675 --> 00:25:27,509
What?

478
00:25:27,890 --> 00:25:29,350
Why are you following me?

479
00:25:30,231 --> 00:25:31,565
I'm not following you, okay?

480
00:25:31,870 --> 00:25:32,996
I'm just accompanying you.

481
00:25:34,829 --> 00:25:36,176
Yeah, totally not obvious.

482
00:25:37,233 --> 00:25:38,254
But why though?

483
00:25:41,385 --> 00:25:42,511
Alright, fine. I'll stop.

484
00:25:43,917 --> 00:25:44,835
Well...

485
00:25:44,860 --> 00:25:47,696
I just want the mugger
and his accomplices to be caught.

486
00:25:48,369 --> 00:25:49,662
So they won’t be able
to victimize anyone else.

487
00:25:50,484 --> 00:25:51,558
Come on.

488
00:25:51,890 --> 00:25:52,824
Let's find them.

489
00:25:55,615 --> 00:25:57,743
Why would I go with you?
I don't even know you.

490
00:25:59,176 --> 00:25:59,885
Estong.

491
00:26:00,065 --> 00:26:00,899
My name's Estong.

492
00:26:03,568 --> 00:26:04,778
So, now you know me.

493
00:26:04,832 --> 00:26:05,968
All goods?

494
00:26:05,993 --> 00:26:06,662
Let's go.

495
00:26:06,687 --> 00:26:07,810
No.

496
00:26:07,835 --> 00:26:09,753
I don't know you.

497
00:26:10,045 --> 00:26:12,980
I don't trust people
that easily, and what if...

498
00:26:13,005 --> 00:26:15,174
you're also one of their accomplices.

499
00:26:15,484 --> 00:26:17,903
Maybe this is just a scheme,

500
00:26:18,070 --> 00:26:19,488
and I'm actually your next victim.

501
00:26:19,724 --> 00:26:24,207
Wow, you're so quick to accuse me
without even a second thought.

502
00:26:24,871 --> 00:26:25,663
Just wow.

503
00:26:29,881 --> 00:26:31,090
I'm just making sure.

504
00:26:31,618 --> 00:26:33,537
So please, stop bothering me.

505
00:26:33,562 --> 00:26:34,730
I'm running out of time.

506
00:26:35,904 --> 00:26:36,488
That wasn't me!

507
00:26:36,513 --> 00:26:39,188
I told you, I'm not
a pusher, just a user!

508
00:26:39,213 --> 00:26:41,027
Spare me your alibis!

509
00:26:46,957 --> 00:26:47,891
Miss?

510
00:26:47,916 --> 00:26:49,126
Miss, are you okay?

511
00:26:58,509 --> 00:26:59,441
Miss?

512
00:27:06,178 --> 00:27:07,097
Miss?

513
00:27:08,253 --> 00:27:09,510
Miss, are you okay?

514
00:27:10,355 --> 00:27:11,129
Miss?

515
00:27:13,269 --> 00:27:14,312
Tristan.

516
00:27:18,906 --> 00:27:19,740
Tristan?

517
00:27:21,921 --> 00:27:23,130
My name is Tristan.

518
00:27:29,162 --> 00:27:30,254
Tristan?

519
00:27:45,690 --> 00:27:48,359
Why so quiet all of a sudden?

520
00:27:49,311 --> 00:27:52,785
Just a while ago, you were in such
a hurry to look for your painting.

521
00:27:58,223 --> 00:27:59,238
Hug me.

522
00:28:02,775 --> 00:28:03,691
Hug?

523
00:28:09,028 --> 00:28:09,792
Alright.

524
00:28:10,443 --> 00:28:11,418
If you say so.

525
00:28:27,030 --> 00:28:28,238
No homo.

526
00:28:38,976 --> 00:28:39,810
Look, miss.

527
00:28:41,088 --> 00:28:42,381
I'll prove to you

528
00:28:42,506 --> 00:28:44,549
that I'm not working with the thieves

529
00:28:44,574 --> 00:28:46,034
who stole your painting.

530
00:28:47,219 --> 00:28:48,220
That painting is gone.

531
00:28:50,694 --> 00:28:52,654
There's no getting it back anymore.

532
00:28:55,042 --> 00:28:56,168
You're so negative.

533
00:28:57,302 --> 00:28:58,301
It's true.

534
00:28:59,799 --> 00:29:02,677
Maybe that's just how
the universe intended it.

535
00:29:04,585 --> 00:29:06,587
That I won't find the painting ever again.

536
00:29:07,705 --> 00:29:08,793
Maybe...

537
00:29:09,997 --> 00:29:12,416
we are not meant to be known for our art.

538
00:29:14,271 --> 00:29:17,121
Uh— "we"...

539
00:29:17,408 --> 00:29:18,535
What do you mean "us"?

540
00:29:19,244 --> 00:29:20,161
Me...

541
00:29:20,917 --> 00:29:22,043
Them...

542
00:29:22,943 --> 00:29:23,840
Us.

543
00:29:30,495 --> 00:29:31,388
Well...

544
00:29:31,413 --> 00:29:33,999
I kind of get what you mean.

545
00:29:35,095 --> 00:29:36,680
Do you ever get that feeling like...

546
00:29:37,269 --> 00:29:39,021
the universe is against you?

547
00:29:39,264 --> 00:29:40,515
That feeling you get when

548
00:29:41,141 --> 00:29:42,559
your girlfriend leaves you,

549
00:29:43,439 --> 00:29:45,608
you get scammed with a bogus overseas job,

550
00:29:46,263 --> 00:29:47,473
you get mugged,

551
00:29:48,096 --> 00:29:51,391
then you get punched in the face
for throwing up on someone.

552
00:29:56,747 --> 00:29:58,499
Wow, your life really sucks.

553
00:30:00,754 --> 00:30:02,297
You sure can throw a punch.

554
00:30:03,879 --> 00:30:04,838
But...

555
00:30:05,112 --> 00:30:07,156
Just like what Popsy Bert told me,

556
00:30:08,075 --> 00:30:10,869
As long as there's breath in us,
there's still fight in us.

557
00:30:11,707 --> 00:30:13,626
So just think positive, okay?

558
00:30:14,625 --> 00:30:15,751
Life goes on...

559
00:30:16,600 --> 00:30:17,601
and on...

560
00:30:17,867 --> 00:30:18,743
and on.

561
00:30:20,936 --> 00:30:21,879
Okay?

562
00:30:26,873 --> 00:30:27,903
So?

563
00:30:27,928 --> 00:30:28,904
Let's go?

564
00:30:29,123 --> 00:30:30,457
Let's find your painting.

565
00:30:31,813 --> 00:30:32,773
I don't want to.

566
00:30:35,352 --> 00:30:37,020
I just want to be by myself.

567
00:30:37,199 --> 00:30:38,409
Just leave me alone.

568
00:30:39,147 --> 00:30:40,690
- You're so confusing.
- Balloon.

569
00:30:41,316 --> 00:30:45,278
Just a while ago, you were so eager to
find your painting, but now...

570
00:30:45,749 --> 00:30:46,834
you're giving up just like that?

571
00:30:47,887 --> 00:30:52,823
Not me. I'm not giving up. I'll find
that mugger and prove I'm innocent.

572
00:30:55,539 --> 00:30:56,665
Where could he be?

573
00:30:56,665 --> 00:30:58,041
Balloons for sale!

574
00:30:58,250 --> 00:31:00,210
Hey, look! Balloons!

575
00:31:00,210 --> 00:31:01,503
Look, there's a balloon over there!

576
00:31:01,503 --> 00:31:02,921
Maybe the mugger's just around here.

577
00:31:03,505 --> 00:31:05,590
- Can I buy a balloon,
- I'd like the heart-shaped one.

578
00:31:06,425 --> 00:31:07,801
You're really going to buy one, huh?

579
00:31:08,301 --> 00:31:09,594
Which one would you like?

580
00:31:10,762 --> 00:31:12,889
- I'll take this one
- You have to pay first!

581
00:31:12,889 --> 00:31:13,723
Thankyou.

582
00:31:13,723 --> 00:31:16,059
Balloon!

583
00:31:16,143 --> 00:31:17,269
- Just one, mister.
- Okay.

584
00:31:17,727 --> 00:31:20,313
Balloon! Yeye wants the big one!

585
00:31:20,338 --> 00:31:22,048
- One big balloon, please!
- Here's a big one, ma'am.

586
00:31:22,732 --> 00:31:23,859
Thank you!

587
00:31:23,859 --> 00:31:25,736
- Balloon!
- Hey! You didn't pay for that!

588
00:31:26,853 --> 00:31:27,395
What?

589
00:31:27,420 --> 00:31:28,463
You need to pay for that balloon.

590
00:31:28,845 --> 00:31:30,555
- Oh, Yeye.
- That's not free, okay?

591
00:31:30,580 --> 00:31:32,374
Yeye has no money.

592
00:31:32,742 --> 00:31:35,245
Okay, but you need to return that.
Nothing's free anymore.

593
00:31:35,245 --> 00:31:37,330
- Balloon!
- You don't even have money!

594
00:31:37,747 --> 00:31:39,666
- I want my balloon!
- You can't pay for it, okay?

595
00:31:39,666 --> 00:31:41,835
- That's my balloon!
- Take it, Mister.

596
00:31:43,086 --> 00:31:44,282
That's enough, okay?
You don't have any money.

597
00:31:44,306 --> 00:31:45,046
And you had to ruin it.

598
00:31:45,046 --> 00:31:48,550
I want my balloon. Yeye
wants her balloon back!

599
00:31:48,550 --> 00:31:52,586
- I said, I want balloon!
- Ouch!

600
00:31:53,447 --> 00:31:57,451
- I told you, I want my balloon!
- Stop it.

601
00:31:57,476 --> 00:31:59,186
You're pushing it!

602
00:32:03,324 --> 00:32:05,576
Balloon!

603
00:32:05,959 --> 00:32:07,002
How much is that?

604
00:32:07,027 --> 00:32:08,620
- One hundred fifty pesos.
- Why so expensive?

605
00:32:08,645 --> 00:32:09,813
That's just how they're priced.

606
00:32:09,988 --> 00:32:10,964
Fine.

607
00:32:10,989 --> 00:32:12,674
Give me the new one, okay?

608
00:32:12,699 --> 00:32:14,451
Balloon!

609
00:32:14,910 --> 00:32:18,121
- I want my balloon!
- Here, I already got it, okay?

610
00:32:20,219 --> 00:32:21,781
You owe me for that, okay?

611
00:32:22,209 --> 00:32:25,212
Balloon!

612
00:32:25,587 --> 00:32:28,048
Thank you!

613
00:32:28,048 --> 00:32:28,982
Balloon.

614
00:32:29,007 --> 00:32:31,218
Balloon!

615
00:32:31,218 --> 00:32:32,636
Hey, don't forget your stuff!

616
00:32:34,471 --> 00:32:36,848
Wow, so you really
didn't include me.

617
00:32:37,599 --> 00:32:40,727
Girls, what's Ysa doing
at the barangay hall?

618
00:32:41,990 --> 00:32:44,118
At the barangay hall? Really?

619
00:32:45,315 --> 00:32:47,359
Yeah, we'll talk about it later.

620
00:32:48,860 --> 00:32:50,403
Why would she need to go to the town hall?

621
00:32:52,781 --> 00:32:54,070
What was that about?

622
00:32:55,040 --> 00:32:56,458
Why can't she tell us?

623
00:32:58,995 --> 00:33:01,665
I know, right? I'm also worried about it.

624
00:33:02,531 --> 00:33:03,578
You know what...

625
00:33:03,674 --> 00:33:07,469
I just hope that she and
her other personalities

626
00:33:07,770 --> 00:33:09,856
can learn to trust us.

627
00:33:09,881 --> 00:33:11,758
I hope they all realize that

628
00:33:11,758 --> 00:33:15,011
we're on their side, no matter what.

629
00:33:16,157 --> 00:33:17,993
Don't think that we've fallen short.

630
00:33:19,256 --> 00:33:21,050
We're doing everything we can.

631
00:33:23,016 --> 00:33:24,211
But admit it.

632
00:33:25,247 --> 00:33:26,957
Is Ysabelle really the reason,

633
00:33:27,606 --> 00:33:28,719
Or...

634
00:33:29,464 --> 00:33:30,453
because...

635
00:33:33,422 --> 00:33:37,259
You were just that into me back in college?

636
00:33:37,284 --> 00:33:39,803
Oh gosh, really, are you serious?

637
00:33:39,828 --> 00:33:43,206
You're the one who asked me out several
times, and I turned you down.

638
00:33:44,230 --> 00:33:45,523
You were just playing hard to get!

639
00:33:45,934 --> 00:33:47,602
But you ended up with me anyway.

640
00:33:47,627 --> 00:33:48,753
Awww!

641
00:33:51,126 --> 00:33:53,587
Alright, go home now. Come back tomorrow!

642
00:33:53,612 --> 00:33:55,780
Hey, nosy people, get out of here!

643
00:33:56,694 --> 00:33:58,488
- Oh, they're so nosy.
- Don't they have anything better to do?

644
00:33:59,531 --> 00:34:00,735
The truth is,

645
00:34:01,246 --> 00:34:04,499
I really saw how much you loved Ysabelle.

646
00:34:04,969 --> 00:34:06,605
That's when I realized

647
00:34:06,605 --> 00:34:09,608
we could really build a family together.

648
00:34:11,168 --> 00:34:15,505
You're right. That's what we promised
our best friends, right?

649
00:34:15,763 --> 00:34:19,684
That we would give their daughter
a good and normal life,

650
00:34:20,336 --> 00:34:23,840
And that we'll love
her like our own. Right?

651
00:34:25,392 --> 00:34:26,586
But...

652
00:34:26,708 --> 00:34:29,961
Why hasn't she gotten better?

653
00:34:30,953 --> 00:34:33,539
Of course, we can't control everything.

654
00:34:34,049 --> 00:34:37,093
There's still so much she's
dealing with emotionally.

655
00:34:37,927 --> 00:34:40,513
Ysabelle is still a work in progress.

656
00:34:40,538 --> 00:34:42,915
Just like her other personalities.

657
00:34:44,768 --> 00:34:48,953
Just as long as we're always there for her.

658
00:34:48,978 --> 00:34:49,604
Right.

659
00:34:49,644 --> 00:34:52,313
Not like that jerk.

660
00:34:52,827 --> 00:34:55,121
Don't ever mention his name.

661
00:34:55,146 --> 00:34:56,564
I know.

662
00:34:57,848 --> 00:34:58,974
Ninong! Ninang!

663
00:34:59,433 --> 00:35:00,601
- Yes?
- What is it, Adel?

664
00:35:01,034 --> 00:35:03,552
Who is this guy now?

665
00:35:03,577 --> 00:35:05,287
Look at the way he looks at Ate Ysa.

666
00:35:07,515 --> 00:35:08,683
He looks like a creep, right?

667
00:35:08,708 --> 00:35:09,617
A creep?

668
00:35:10,440 --> 00:35:11,438
A creep?

669
00:35:12,633 --> 00:35:14,176
This guy? A creep?!

670
00:35:14,410 --> 00:35:15,969
This guy looks familiar!

671
00:35:17,108 --> 00:35:18,234
Hey, that's just you!

672
00:35:18,259 --> 00:35:19,511
- That's just me?
- Yes!

673
00:35:19,511 --> 00:35:22,055
- No, it's not that.
- You know I only have eyes for you, right?

674
00:35:22,639 --> 00:35:23,953
Can you stop?

675
00:35:24,755 --> 00:35:25,881
Here, look at this.

676
00:35:37,167 --> 00:35:39,381
Whoa, hey. Wait, hold on.

677
00:35:39,601 --> 00:35:40,393
Hey!

678
00:35:41,741 --> 00:35:42,926
Hey, wait.

679
00:35:42,951 --> 00:35:44,369
Why, what do you want?

680
00:35:44,369 --> 00:35:46,750
Hey, don't forget about what you owe.

681
00:35:46,815 --> 00:35:49,234
The one fifty pesos I paid
for your balloon, Tristan.

682
00:35:49,985 --> 00:35:51,737
I told you, my name is Yeye.

683
00:35:52,852 --> 00:35:53,750
Yeye?

684
00:35:54,713 --> 00:35:56,602
You know, I've been so
confused this whole time.

685
00:35:57,340 --> 00:36:00,927
Earlier, you wanted to find your painting,
so you went to the town hall.

686
00:36:01,553 --> 00:36:05,241
And now, your mood suddenly changed.
I don't understand you anymore.

687
00:36:05,266 --> 00:36:06,641
Are you on something?

688
00:36:08,449 --> 00:36:09,406
Lollipop.

689
00:36:09,690 --> 00:36:10,648
Want some?

690
00:36:11,609 --> 00:36:13,193
Wait a minute. Just hold on.

691
00:36:13,753 --> 00:36:14,962
Here we go again!

692
00:36:14,987 --> 00:36:17,323
It's my fault, right? I'm
always the one to blame?!

693
00:36:23,366 --> 00:36:25,802
You're always blaming me for everything!
That's just how you are, right?!

694
00:36:25,827 --> 00:36:29,956
Oh my God, what is this?

695
00:36:29,956 --> 00:36:31,578
Where am I this time?

696
00:36:32,297 --> 00:36:33,962
Ugh! What is this?

697
00:36:34,591 --> 00:36:36,092
Where am I?

698
00:36:36,117 --> 00:36:37,911
- What happened?
- There goes my one fifty pesos.

699
00:36:39,519 --> 00:36:40,523
What happened to you?

700
00:36:44,120 --> 00:36:47,540
Adel! Adel! Oh my gosh!

701
00:36:48,662 --> 00:36:50,163
That lollipop is hitting real hard!

702
00:36:50,452 --> 00:36:52,045
Hey, you're ditching me, aren't you?

703
00:36:52,070 --> 00:36:55,774
OMG! There are new
arrivals! I'm so excited!

704
00:36:55,774 --> 00:36:56,566
Ate Ysa!

705
00:36:56,566 --> 00:36:59,945
Love these! They're so beautiful!

706
00:37:00,815 --> 00:37:02,233
Girl, I've been looking everywhere for you.

707
00:37:02,258 --> 00:37:04,199
I've been here calling out to you, but you
didn't even notice me.

708
00:37:04,453 --> 00:37:06,372
- So nice!
- Where have you been?

709
00:37:06,509 --> 00:37:09,047
Auntie and Uncle have been waiting for
you for a while now.

710
00:37:09,310 --> 00:37:09,899
Oh.

711
00:37:09,924 --> 00:37:12,508
Wait, I'll tell them
that you're here now.

712
00:37:13,833 --> 00:37:15,960
I actually can't remember...

713
00:37:15,960 --> 00:37:18,588
But you already know what happens when
the others take over.

714
00:37:19,372 --> 00:37:20,998
I don't know what to do anymore.

715
00:37:21,023 --> 00:37:22,108
You're ditching me, aren't you?

716
00:37:22,275 --> 00:37:23,568
Wait, I know you.

717
00:37:23,865 --> 00:37:24,508
Huh?

718
00:37:24,673 --> 00:37:25,799
I've never seen you before.

719
00:37:26,222 --> 00:37:27,515
I can't be mistaken.

720
00:37:28,566 --> 00:37:31,694
You're the one in the picture with Ate Ysa
from the town hall.

721
00:37:32,554 --> 00:37:34,347
Hey, are you stalking her?

722
00:37:36,354 --> 00:37:37,355
What do you mean 'stalker'?

723
00:37:37,594 --> 00:37:38,637
I'm not a stalker, okay?

724
00:37:38,662 --> 00:37:39,955
We know each other, okay?

725
00:37:40,682 --> 00:37:41,805
- You know him?
- Huh?

726
00:37:42,827 --> 00:37:43,912
I don't know you.

727
00:37:44,255 --> 00:37:45,381
I've never seen you before.

728
00:37:45,564 --> 00:37:46,649
She doesn't know you.

729
00:37:46,674 --> 00:37:49,427
What do you mean you don't know me?
We've been together this whole time.

730
00:37:49,689 --> 00:37:52,025
Isn't your name Tristan?

731
00:37:52,050 --> 00:37:53,593
Ah, no, no. Uh..

732
00:37:53,832 --> 00:37:54,891
Yeye!

733
00:37:55,103 --> 00:37:56,328
Excuse me?

734
00:37:56,787 --> 00:37:59,040
No! My beautiful name is...

735
00:37:59,260 --> 00:38:00,218
Cacai!

736
00:38:02,925 --> 00:38:03,938
Cacai?

737
00:38:04,717 --> 00:38:05,902
You must be a scammer.

738
00:38:06,111 --> 00:38:07,612
Is that why you keep changing your name?

739
00:38:07,637 --> 00:38:11,474
- Mister, just go, you can leave now.
- You're a scammer, huh?

740
00:38:11,474 --> 00:38:13,977
No, I need to clear something
up with her first because—

741
00:38:14,266 --> 00:38:15,705
You can do it next time.

742
00:38:15,730 --> 00:38:17,732
It's also about her stolen painting.

743
00:38:19,072 --> 00:38:22,117
O to the M to the G!

744
00:38:22,933 --> 00:38:25,203
The painting is missing?!

745
00:38:25,796 --> 00:38:26,881
Mister, just go, please!

746
00:38:26,906 --> 00:38:28,032
But didn't we look for—

747
00:38:28,032 --> 00:38:30,326
Mister, just go, now!

748
00:38:30,326 --> 00:38:32,954
- Just leave us be!
- Oh my!

749
00:38:32,979 --> 00:38:36,374
- Just leave us, please!
- She still owes me a hundred fifty pesos.

750
00:38:36,916 --> 00:38:37,876
Buddy, do we have a problem?

751
00:38:37,876 --> 00:38:38,960
Yes, he's causing trouble!

752
00:38:38,960 --> 00:38:41,337
- Just go! We don't need you here.
- Oh, I don't have a problem, sir.

753
00:38:41,337 --> 00:38:42,755
- Just go! We don't need you here.
- She still owes me money.

754
00:38:42,755 --> 00:38:43,840
- Just leave her to us!
- He's causing trouble?

755
00:38:43,840 --> 00:38:44,883
- Just go, now!
- No, there's no problem here.

756
00:38:44,883 --> 00:38:45,563
Just go, now!

757
00:38:45,587 --> 00:38:47,652
It seems like you're
causing problems here.

758
00:38:47,677 --> 00:38:50,013
Leave! Can't you just
come back some other time?

759
00:38:50,013 --> 00:38:51,931
Go! Just leave her to us and let her be.

760
00:38:51,931 --> 00:38:52,802
Hey!

761
00:38:52,827 --> 00:38:54,409
What are you doing to Adel?!

762
00:38:54,434 --> 00:38:55,211
Huh?

763
00:38:56,827 --> 00:38:59,205
Hey, I know you! You look familiar!

764
00:38:59,497 --> 00:39:01,124
You stole the painting, didn't you?!

765
00:39:01,477 --> 00:39:02,728
Oh no, it's Kuya Bogart.

766
00:39:03,391 --> 00:39:03,943
Bogart?

767
00:39:03,943 --> 00:39:07,113
What are you doing here? What are you
doing to Adel? Why are you harassing her?

768
00:39:07,113 --> 00:39:08,239
Hey, I'm not harassing anyone.

769
00:39:08,239 --> 00:39:09,240
Hey! Hey! Hey!

770
00:39:09,240 --> 00:39:10,491
Who's harassing my daughter?

771
00:39:10,491 --> 00:39:12,327
This one right here, he's the creep!

772
00:39:12,327 --> 00:39:13,836
This guy's such a creep!
He's causing trouble here!

773
00:39:13,860 --> 00:39:14,913
I'm not. I didn't do anything!

774
00:39:14,913 --> 00:39:17,040
He's causing trouble here! Jerk!

775
00:39:17,206 --> 00:39:19,709
Wait, isn't he the guy we saw in our
group chat? So he's a creep after all!

776
00:39:19,709 --> 00:39:21,002
Hey, you! Leave now!

777
00:39:21,002 --> 00:39:22,837
You're mistaken, I
didn't do anything to her—

778
00:39:22,837 --> 00:39:24,647
Stay away from her! What's your problem?

779
00:39:24,672 --> 00:39:26,184
You're not leaving?

780
00:39:26,209 --> 00:39:27,335
So you're not leaving, huh?!

781
00:39:28,801 --> 00:39:30,178
I told you to leave!

782
00:39:30,500 --> 00:39:31,492
Where's Bogart?

783
00:39:31,763 --> 00:39:32,758
Where's Bogart?

784
00:39:43,566 --> 00:39:44,692
That's enough!

785
00:39:58,931 --> 00:40:02,393
Stop it, please!

786
00:40:02,418 --> 00:40:03,252
Stop it!

787
00:40:03,378 --> 00:40:04,963
He's my friend!

788
00:40:37,495 --> 00:40:38,788
My best friend!

789
00:40:39,205 --> 00:40:40,456
- Best friend!
- Ysa!

790
00:40:41,457 --> 00:40:42,667
Ysa!

791
00:40:45,545 --> 00:40:46,546
Estong!

792
00:41:13,021 --> 00:41:14,356
Get out of the way!

793
00:41:20,493 --> 00:41:21,329
Yeye?

794
00:41:24,580 --> 00:41:25,706
It's just me now. Ysa.

795
00:41:26,066 --> 00:41:27,150
A different name?

796
00:41:28,921 --> 00:41:29,681
Um...

797
00:41:30,898 --> 00:41:32,211
I have...

798
00:41:32,616 --> 00:41:34,827
Dissociative Identity Disorder.

799
00:41:36,222 --> 00:41:38,516
I have different personalities.

800
00:41:46,105 --> 00:41:47,148
It's confirmed.

801
00:41:47,661 --> 00:41:49,287
She's no ordinary woman.

802
00:41:54,572 --> 00:41:56,074
The ones you've met

803
00:41:56,074 --> 00:41:58,743
are four of my six dominant personalities.

804
00:41:58,743 --> 00:41:59,619
What?

805
00:42:00,561 --> 00:42:01,312
Six?

806
00:42:01,337 --> 00:42:03,164
I'd also like to apologize.

807
00:42:03,164 --> 00:42:04,791
We are one family here,

808
00:42:04,791 --> 00:42:05,416
- okay?
- Right.

809
00:42:05,416 --> 00:42:07,810
Why do you think our street was named...

810
00:42:07,977 --> 00:42:10,897
Nagkaisang Bayan Street.

811
00:42:10,922 --> 00:42:12,090
What are you doing here?

812
00:42:12,090 --> 00:42:13,091
This is our café.

813
00:42:13,091 --> 00:42:14,217
I'm on duty right now.

814
00:42:14,217 --> 00:42:14,842
Wait.

815
00:42:14,842 --> 00:42:16,679
Could you be the one who took the painting?

816
00:42:16,704 --> 00:42:19,989
Maybe you made up those other
accomplices just to throw us off!

817
00:42:20,014 --> 00:42:21,224
Are you looking for me?

818
00:42:21,224 --> 00:42:21,891
Keep dreaming.

819
00:42:21,891 --> 00:42:23,059
You know, it feels like

820
00:42:23,269 --> 00:42:25,354
they're all returning
to how they used to be.

821
00:42:25,761 --> 00:42:28,222
She's getting triggered so easily again.

822
00:42:29,152 --> 00:42:31,613
You know, it's really that man's fault.

823
00:42:31,926 --> 00:42:34,971
We're not supposed to mention
that man's name, okay?

824
00:42:36,478 --> 00:42:37,548
Does he have a crush on Ate Ysa?

825
00:42:37,573 --> 00:42:39,414
No! That can't happen!

826
00:42:39,439 --> 00:42:41,338
I don't think I can handle another
complicated woman, bro.

827
00:42:41,363 --> 00:42:42,781
I just got out of one, remember?

828
00:42:45,336 --> 00:42:47,213
Dear, isn't that the mugger?

829
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:49,125
Hey, you!

830
00:42:49,150 --> 00:42:50,375
Come here!

831
00:42:50,400 --> 00:42:51,025
You!

832
00:42:52,587 --> 00:42:53,704
Hey!
